    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.ai\n\n### Description\n\nI have LazyVim installed which is using mini.ai module. When going to the mini.ai help file to learn and test the module it is not selecting the expected objects.\r\n\r\nOn line 159 of the help file. When I hover the cursor over the `*` and type `vit` it is expected to select the `*` character at position 4 as expected however it instead jumps to select the `b` character at position 12.\r\n\r\nFor context:\r\n```\r\n|---|---------------|-1234567890123456-|--------|--------|--------|--------|\r\n| t |      Tag      | <x>*</x><y>b</y> | [1;8]  | [4;4]  | [9;16] |[12;12] |\r\n```\r\n\r\nI noticed that the highlighting of the tags is very weird where just hovering over the `b` character it naturally hint highlights from position 5 to 16. I assume this is from something like treesitter which may not be correctly parsing out the tags.\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.9.1\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nCurrently using LazyVim but can try to put together a minimal config if not reproducable. Would be nice if you could supply me with a minimal lua config as I was having an issue getting mini.ai working with that as the only plugin for lazy.vim\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nSelect the text as described int he help file.\n\n### Actual behavior\n\nHighlighting a different part of the text.",
